.TH Install-Docker 1 "December 2025" "Noble Factor" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
Install-Docker \- install Docker Engine, CLI, containerd, buildx, and compose plugin
.SH SYNOPSIS
Install-Docker [OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Installs Docker CE, CLI, containerd, buildx, and compose plugin. Handles removal of conflicting packages. Includes special instructions for ODROID and Raspberry Pi hardware. Supports both Debian and Ubuntu systems. Automatically detects architecture and installs appropriate packages.
.IP \(bu 2
Removes conflicting packages (docker.io, docker-doc, docker-compose, docker-compose-v2, podman-docker, containerd, runc)
.IP \(bu 2
Performs system cleanup with apt-get autoremove and update
.IP \(bu 2
Installs docker-ce, docker-ce-cli, containerd.io, docker-buildx-plugin, docker-compose-plugin, and lshw
.IP \(bu 2
Verifies installation by running 'sudo docker run hello-world'
.IP \(bu 2
Detects hardware platform and provides special instructions for ODROID C4/C5 devices
.PP
For ODROID C4/C5 devices, the script checks for required systemd cgroup hierarchy configuration in /media/boot/boot.ini and provides manual setup instructions if needed.
.PP
This script must be run with sudo/root privileges.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show usage information and exit.
.TP
.B --no-install-recommends
Install only essential packages, omitting recommended extras.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Show actions without making changes.
.TP
.B --force
Force reinstallation of Docker packages.
.SH USAGE
.RS
.nf
\fBsudo ./bin/Install-Docker [OPTIONS]\fR
.fi
.RE
.SH HARDWARE SUPPORT
.TP
.B ODROID C4/C5
Requires systemd.unified_cgroup_hierarchy=0 boot parameter. The script provides instructions for manual configuration if needed.
.TP
.B Raspberry Pi 5
Fully supported without special configuration.
.TP
.B Other platforms
Untested but should work on standard x86_64 and ARM systems.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Success - Docker installed and verified
.TP
1
Error during installation or verification
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.TP
.B Required:
sudo, apt-get, dpkg, lshw, jq
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR docker (1),
.BR containerd (8)
.PP
Docker installation guide: https://docs.docker.com/engine/install/ubuntu/
